# Machine agent framework (Codex)

The registry at `{{REPO_DIR}}/roles.config.json` is the single source of truth
for every agent profile on this machine. Each profile is installed here as an
`agent-<key>` skill.

{{ROSTER_SENTENCE}}

{{ROSTER_TABLE}}

## What Codex can and cannot do with this framework

**Can:** adopt any profile (load its `agent-<key>` skill and work inside it),
run the deterministic router, delegate with `spawn_agent`, and run a real code
review with the native `codex review` subcommand.

Ordinary work stays in the current Codex session. Planner -> Builder and its
component roles require explicit invocation; task size and router output never
start them. Both roles currently use the registry's Astra model at `xhigh`.
Automatic profile selection and post-workflow audit are disabled.

**Direct adoption does not route a model.** A profile adopted in-session uses
that session's actual model. When David explicitly requests a configured
profile dispatch, set its registry model and effort on `spawn_agent` and report
an unavailable route instead of substituting another harness or model.

In an already-user-authorized task, the parent orchestrator may dispatch the
selected configured child with its model, effort, mission, boundaries, and output
contract without another confirmation. That parent dispatch is not a worker's
delegation right. `spawn_agent` gives a child a fresh context, not a profile, so
the parent must include those instructions in its task.

A worker's `canDelegate` and `delegateTo` govern only that worker's nested
handoffs. A router recommendation, a new profile selection, or new authority
still requires user confirmation; an existing authorized parent dispatch does
not.

The `tools:` list in each profile is descriptive vocabulary. Codex does
not enforce it, so a read-only profile's boundary is a discipline here, not a
sandbox. A read-only worker must not edit, write, commit, install, save lessons,
or run mutating checks; it reports useful lesson suggestions unless the task
specifically authorizes a `LESSONS.md` write.

## Picking a profile

- **`runner`** is the everyday front door for routine work, maintenance, and triage.
- **`planner` → `builder`** runs only when David explicitly invokes it; it is never an automatic development step.
- **`code-reviewer`** is optional and runs only when David explicitly requests
  an automated review. It is never a PR gate; David reviews and merges PRs in
  GitHub.
- Direct-call-only profiles ({{DIRECT_CALL_ONLY}}) run only when the user asks
  for them by name.

