## Reviewing and auditing

Requested Code Review and Audit remain available on their registry models.
Automatic post-workflow audit is disabled; no automatic child or verdict is required.

## Rules that do not change per harness

- The registry is the only place a model assignment changes:
  `python3 {{REPO_DIR}}/apply.py set <role-or-agent> <class>`. Never hand-edit a
  generated skill file — the next install overwrites it.
- The router recommends; a new profile selection or new authority needs user
  confirmation. Do not repeat that question for an already-authorized parent dispatch.
- Direct-call-only profiles are never automatic routing destinations.

Codex is the only supported harness. dsh, Pi, Hermes, Gemini, and Claude
adapters are decommissioned and must not be installed, invoked, or used as fallback.
